<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Grenland</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom at the mouth of the Skien river in southern Norway, one of the coastal realms brought under Harald Fairhair.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Grenland, around the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skienselva">Skienselva</a> and the coast of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telemark">Telemark</a>, appears in the sagas as one of the small kingdoms of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. Its early history is obscure and known only from scattered references in later Icelandic writings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The district looked to the sea and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skagerrak">Skagerrak</a>, and its people farmed, fished and traded. Inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telemark">Telemark</a> supplied iron and whetstones that were exported widely in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>. No reliable record of its kings or institutions survives.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Grenland passed into the realm of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vestfold">Vestfold</a> kings and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> in the late 9th century and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>. The town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skien">Skien</a> grew there in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar"